  <prompt>Port H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs's 3 collaborators: (1) AzCliKvSecretsWriter (keyvault secret set/show/delete + account show, AzCliKvSecretsWriter.cs:129-231) -&gt; Azure.Security.KeyVault.Secrets.SecretClient (SetSecretAsync/GetSecretAsync/StartDeleteSecretAsync); 'account show' becomes ArmClient.GetDefaultSubscription(); (2) AzCliAppServiceIdentityPatcher (webapp update / webapp deployment slot update, AzCliAppServiceIdentityPatcher.cs:58,78 -- THIS IS THE T1 OWNER) -&gt; Azure.ResourceManager.AppService WebSiteResource.UpdateAsync(new SitePatchInfo{KeyVaultReferenceIdentity=uamiId}), SAME on WebSiteSlotResource (BOTH slots, per this project's MUST rule: 'MUST PATCH App Service keyVaultReferenceIdentity to UAMI on both slots'); (3) AzCliSlotIdentityRoleGranter (webapp show + role assignment create, AzCliSlotIdentityRoleGranter.cs:103-154 -- THIS IS THE T5 OWNER) -&gt; Azure.ResourceManager.Authorization RoleAssignmentCollection.CreateOrUpdateAsync(roleAssignmentName, principalId, roleDefinitionId). PRESERVE the existing never-delete guard logic (already correct per DS-4 -- core real).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Azure.Security.KeyVault.Secrets.SecretClient, Azure.ResourceManager.AppService SitePatchInfo.KeyVaultReferenceIdentity (both slots), and Azure.ResourceManager.Authorization role-assignment creation.</role>

  <goal>H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs's 3 collaborators are pure .NET SDK implementations. The never-delete guard (already correct, DS-4 confirms) is UNCHANGED. T1 (KeyVaultReferenceIdentity PATCH on BOTH production and staging slots) and T5 (role-assignment grant) are performed via typed ARM SDK calls with a post-PATCH ARM read verifying the value actually landed (per this project's existing escalation-trigger convention for task 047's H4 risk item -- 'ARM read post-PATCH; escalation trigger in POML').</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §2 (H4 row) states: 'core real (never-delete guard, T1/T5) BUT (a) StaticKvSecretManifest interim still bound... and (b) AzCliKvSecretsWriter.ResolveValueForEntry writes literal {name}-interim-placeholder-{customerId} VALUES -- even with az present, KV receives non-functional secrets.' THIS task (125) addresses the SDK-port half only (the mechanical collaborator swap); task 126 addresses the real-value-sourcing + manifest-swap half (the brownfield correctness fix). DS-4 calls H4 'THE CORRECTNESS GATE -- currently writes literal placeholder values, breaking every downstream secret consumer' and DS-4 §4 places it in Wave G-2 explicitly because 'H4 correctness (real secret values) is prerequisite for everything after.'</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/H4KvSecretsPopulationHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/SecretClientKvWriter.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/ArmAppServiceIdentityPatcher.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/ArmSlotIdentityRoleGranter.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="102" status="pending">wave-sequencing</dependency>
      <dependency task="103" status="pending">H4 keyed registration</dependency>
      <dependency task="123" status="pending">H2a must have deployed the App Service + KV resources this handler populates/patches</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design.md §4.1b">Handler runtime classification (Option D hybrid, DS-1b Sec.2): 12 handlers are pure .NET SDK/REST under DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the L2 UAMI (Class A); H14a is the sole Class-C residual (Exchange sidecar); H7/H10/H11/H12c are already native. No ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may remain in this handler's target state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md MUST rules (post-line-254 block)">No new ProcessStartInfo/shell-out collaborator may be introduced by this task. Option D's entire point is deleting the pwsh/az/pac dependency from the L2 runtime, not adding to it (the sole designed exception is the H14a Exchange sidecar).</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md project MUST rules">MUST PATCH App Service keyVaultReferenceIdentity to UAMI on BOTH slots (T1) -- do not patch production only. MUST verify the PATCH landed via a post-PATCH ARM read (this project's existing escalation-trigger convention for H4's risk item).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §2 H4 row">PRESERVE the existing never-delete guard logic unchanged -- it is already correct. This task's scope is the 3 collaborator SDK ports, NOT a redesign of the guard.</constraint>
    <constraint source="auth-v4 coordination (spec.md FR-39, added v3.5 2026-08-19; notes/AUTH-V4-CHANGE-REQUEST-RESPONSE.md)">The `BFF-API-ClientSecret` KV secret-SEEDING path is DEPRECATED going forward -- `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI` owns its retirement schedule (phased rollout with the secret retained as an ordered fallback through their Phase 5). This task's SecretClient/ARM.AppService/ARM.Authorization port covers the OTHER KV secrets H4 populates (webhook signing keys, integration secrets, etc.) plus T1/T5 -- those paths are UNCHANGED by this constraint. Do NOT special-case or remove `BFF-API-ClientSecret` handling in this task; per FR-39's pluggability contract, the seeding path MUST remain runnable during the transition even though the value it writes may not be actively consumed by a FIC-migrated BFF (task 126 owns the real-value-vs-sentinel branching for that specific secret).</constraint>
  </constraints>

