  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read ADR-028's 21 MUSTs plus the 3 existing az-CLI collaborator files in full.</step>
    <step order="1" name="SecretClientKvWriter">Port AzCliKvSecretsWriter's set/show/delete operations to SecretClient; port 'account show' to ArmClient.GetDefaultSubscription(). PRESERVE the never-delete guard's call sites unchanged.</step>
    <step order="2" name="T1 patcher">Author ArmAppServiceIdentityPatcher using WebSiteResource.UpdateAsync(new SitePatchInfo{KeyVaultReferenceIdentity=uamiResourceId}) for production AND the equivalent WebSiteSlotResource call for staging -- BOTH slots, unconditionally.</step>
    <step order="3" name="T1 verify">After each PATCH, perform an ARM read confirming Data.KeyVaultReferenceIdentity now equals the UAMI resource id -- fail loudly (not silently) if the PATCH did not take effect.</step>
    <step order="4" name="T5 granter">Author ArmSlotIdentityRoleGranter using RoleAssignmentCollection.CreateOrUpdateAsync(roleAssignmentName, principalId, roleDefinitionId) for the KV-access role at the appropriate scope.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Wire up">Replace the 3 az-CLI collaborators in H4's owning module with the new SDK implementations.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Tests">T1/T5 tests + never-delete guard regression tests against SDK fakes, per DS-4 §7's test-effort note.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green; grep 'ProcessStartInfo\|az ' in the 3 new files returns 0 matches.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the post-PATCH ARM read (step 3) shows KeyVaultReferenceIdentity did NOT take effect on either slot after a successful-looking PATCH call, STOP and escalate immediately per this project's existing risk-register entry for task 047/H4 ('keyVaultReferenceIdentity PATCH silently fails (T1)') — this is the exact silent-fail class the project exists to eliminate; do not retry silently or downgrade to a warning.</trigger>
    <trigger>Auth-v4 coordination (FR-39): if `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI`'s secret-retirement Phase 5 lands (i.e., `BFF-API-ClientSecret` is formally retired and no longer an ordered fallback) BEFORE this task executes, STOP and escalate to confirm with the project owner whether this task's scope should drop `BFF-API-ClientSecret` handling entirely rather than porting a seeding path for a secret that no longer exists -- do not silently port dead code.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/SecretClientKvWriter.cs</output>
