  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'ProcessStartInfo' in the 3 new collaborator files returns 0 matches.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T1 test: after ArmAppServiceIdentityPatcher runs, a read of BOTH production and staging slot's Data.KeyVaultReferenceIdentity equals the UAMI resource id.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T1 negative test: if a simulated PATCH fails to take effect (fake ARM response shows unchanged identity), the handler surfaces a Fail/InfraFault outcome, not a silent Pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T5 test: ArmSlotIdentityRoleGranter's CreateOrUpdateAsync call is verified against a fake with the correct roleDefinitionId + principalId + scope.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The never-delete guard's existing test suite passes unmodified against the new SecretClientKvWriter (behavior-preserving swap for that logic).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The `BFF-API-ClientSecret` KV-secret-seeding call path remains runnable end-to-end through this task's SDK port (per FR-39 pluggability during auth-v4's phased rollout) -- no code branch in the 3 new collaborators special-cases or short-circuits that specific secret name.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- the never-delete guard logic + T1/T5 orchestration are already correct in the handler; only the 3 az-CLI collaborators need SDK ports. Extension -- swapping collaborators behind the existing interfaces, preserving the correct guard logic, is the minimal correct move. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H4 cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell main site; separately, T1/T5 stay parsed-stdout-fragile (the exact silent-fail class DS-2b's OCC analysis and this project's whole silent-fail-trap catalog exist to eliminate) rather than typed-SDK-verified.</notes>

